Z||000000||fiero56||03-03-2000||08:08 PM||||Anyone ever hear what happend to this car, or the guy that won it?<BR>I've always wondered. <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/lastfiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/lastfiero.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||03-03-2000||10:07 PM||||Hope for his sake he was smart enough to hang on to it! Lucky Guy!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||03-03-2000||11:26 PM||||As far as I know he still own it.  He tried selling it several years ago, but got no takers.  The asking price?  $50,000!<P>Here's a little tid-bit...the next to last '88 Fiero (identical to the last one) now has a V-8 in it.  I personally think that's a shame....by to each his own I guess. ||||reg||7
Z||000003||fiero56||03-03-2000||11:58 PM||||That's quite a bit of money for a Fiero. But you have to consider what this car means to him and the employees that worked at the plant. This car represented so much more to the employees than just a job and a product. Anyone who has never read "Comback, the Fall and Rise of the American Autmobile Industry" really should. It has a section detailing the life of the Fiero. Very informative, not only on the car, but on the "new age" ideas that came about because of the Fiero project, and changed the thinking of the industry.<P>Where is the car now, what state? Would be nice if there were a more recent article on the man and the car.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GT||03-04-2000||12:57 AM||||Whenever I read any articles of the Fiero history, It always makes me so mad at how the car was created.  The budget GM allowed Pontiac to work with was pathetic and already had the new project doomed before it ever went in to production.  With the money they did have to use, they did well with it, but they obviously could have used more.  I think the fiero project should be in some kind of movie that looks at the project from behind the scenes from beginning to the end in 88.  I think GM today needs to generate some more excitement attention getter cars.  The Corvette is the flashiest but of course you have to have big $$$$.  The Camaro and Firebird/TA are nice but not a stand out automobile like the fiero was.  Toyota is definately got it together when it comes to grabbing attention with the new MR2 and Celica.  I personally do not think GM will ever come out with a mid-engine car again.  If they do, the media will jump on them about the first time they tried a mid-engine car.  ||||reg||1
